meta {
  name: 03 Get Effective Technician Settings
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/technician-settings/effective
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the same effective technician settings as GET /technician-settings", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("tatWarningMinutes");
    expect(d).to.have.property("authoritySignatures");
    expect(d).to.have.property("signatoryBasis");
    expect(d).to.have.property("tatAdjustmentReasons");
    expect(d).to.have.property("isUsefulForEditable");
    expect(d).to.have.property("isOverallResultEditable");
  });
}

docs {
  Effective technician (laboratory) settings for the active branch, for the
  screens that APPLY them: the technician worklist (Approve signatory count),
  result entry (Notes / Overall Result editability) and TAT details (Adjust TAT
  reasons). Same object as `GET /technician-settings`.

  **Login-only - no permission required.** The `View Laboratory Settings` /
  `Update Laboratory Settings` permissions guard only the Laboratory Settings
  page (`GET` / `PUT /technician-settings`). They control access to that page,
  never whether the saved settings apply: a user without them still gets the
  saved values here (not a 403 that made the screens fall back to defaults).

  Never changes saved values. Like `GET /technician-settings`, a branch that has
  never saved settings gets its row created with the module defaults.
}
